[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:The Best Art Critics]
[00:01.34]Who is the student's best critic? | 谁是学生最好的评论家？
[00:15.04]I am an art student and I paint a lot of pictures. | 我是一名艺术生，画了很多画。
[00:21.03]Many people pretend that they understand modern art. | 许多人假装他们懂现代艺术。
[00:26.04]They always tell you what a picture is 'about'. | 他们总是告诉你一幅画是“关于”什么的。
[00:30.26]Of course, many pictures are not 'about' anything. | 当然，许多画根本就不是“关于”什么的。
[00:35.12]They are just pretty patterns. | 它们只是漂亮的图案。
[00:37.66]We like them in the same way that we like pretty curtain material. | 我们喜欢它们的方式，就像我们喜欢漂亮的窗帘布料一样。
[00:43.61]I think that young children often appreciate modern pictures better than anyone else. | 我认为小孩子往往比任何人都更能欣赏现代画。
[00:51.75]They notice more. | 他们注意到更多。
[00:53.78]My sister is only seven, | 我的妹妹只有七岁，
[00:56.84]but she always tells me whether my pictures are good or not. | 但她总是告诉我我的画好不好。
[01:02.17]She came into my room yesterday. | 昨天她进了我的房间。
[01:05.53]'What are you doing?' she asked. | “你在做什么？”她问。
[01:09.03]'I'm hanging this picture on the wall,' I answered. 'It's a new one. Do you like it?' | “我正在把这幅画挂在墙上，”我回答。“这是一幅新画。你喜欢吗？”
[01:17.02]She looked at it critically for a moment. | 她批判性地看了一会儿。
[01:20.76]'It's all right,' she said, 'but isn't it upside down?' | “还行，”她说，“但这幅画是不是倒着挂的？”
[01:26.44]I looked at it again. | 我又看了一遍。
[01:28.88]She was right! It was! | 她是对的！确实是！